 episodes, the case study did provide insight into the predictive ability of accident types in foretelling hit-and-run)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 89.88 Td /TT0 11.82 Tf (incidents. An example of a moderate relationship between the number of passenger automobiles and parties engaged in accidents was)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 75.40 Td /TT0 11.82 Tf (highlighted by the correlational matrix.)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 60.92 Td /TT0 11.82 Tf (Comprehensive provincial analysis also showed significant differences in accident categories, fatalities, and time trends. For example, Noord-)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 46.44 Td /TT0 11.82 Tf (Brabant showed some patterns, such as a high frequency of "head/tail" incidents on straight roads. Regardless of the age of the victims, Fridays)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 31.96 Td /TT0 11.82 Tf (were regularly recorded as having the largest number of accidents and casualties, according to the temporal study. Together, these data present a)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 17.48 Td /TT0 11.82 Tf (comprehensive picture of the dynamics of traffic accidents in the Netherlands, which is helpful for stakeholders and policymakers who want to)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 3.00 Td /TT0 11.82 Tf (improve road safety regulations and reduce particular hazards related to certain variables and geographical areas.)Tj ET Q Q Q Q q 23.52 335.04 758.40 178.08 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 24.00 335.52 cm Q Q q 23.52 335.04 758.40 178.08 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 24.00 335.52 cm Q Q q 23.52 335.04 758.40 178.08 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 24.00 335.52 cm Q Q q 3.36 538.08 798.72 17.28 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 3.84 538.56 cm q -0.48 -0.48 798.72 17.28 re W* n q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 365.98 3.43